          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            While it is straightforward to define an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+site"} internal site
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain"} domain
            of an internal (pre)sheaf, the definition of the codomain is slightly more subtle, for that needs to be a copy of the ambient
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universe"} universe
            internalized into itself. One way to naturally say this is by passing to the
            %em external
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-sheaves"} 2-sheaves
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-topos"} 2-topos
          %ul
            %li
              %em>
                %a{:href => "#InTermsOf2Sheaves"} In terms of external 2-sheaves
              \.
          %p But the resulting notion can of course be expressed entirely in terms of data in the ambient topos. This we spell out in
          %ul
            %li
              %em>
                %a{:href => "#ExplicitDefinition"} Explicit definition
              \.
          %h3#InTermsOf2Sheaves In terms of external 2-sheaves
