              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudofunctor"} pseudofunctor
              which sends an object to the corresponding
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+topos"} slice topos
              and morphisms to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} base change
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi 𝒮
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo ↦
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒮
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\bar \mathcal{S} : X \mapsto \mathcal{S}_{/X}
            %p
              (also called the “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indexed+category"} self-indexing
              of
              = succeed "\u201D)." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒮
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              This is the incarnation of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒮
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
              itself, regard internal to its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-sheaf"} 2-sheaf
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-topos"} 2-topos
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mover
                          %mi Sh
